<figure class="continuation" data-continuation aria-labelledby="r07-cont-title">
 <figcaption id="r07-cont-title"><span>Figure 1</span> The second page after the list changes</figcaption>
 <p>First response, before any change: <strong>101, 102</strong>. The boundary is order 102 at 14 October, 16:05 UTC.</p>
 <div class="choices"><label>Between requests <select data-change><option value="none">No change</option><option value="cancel">101 is cancelled</option><option value="move">103 moves before 102</option></select></label><label>Continue with <select data-method><option value="offset">OFFSET 2</option><option value="key">After the saved key</option></select></label></div>
 <div class="current"><p>Eligible order IDs now, earliest first</p><ol data-orders><li>101</li><li>102</li><li>103</li><li>105</li><li>106</li></ol></div>
 <div class="answer"><p>Second response</p><strong data-answer>103, 105</strong></div>
 <p data-explanation aria-live="polite">The list has not changed. Skipping two rows and continuing after order 102 return the same next two orders.</p>
 <details><summary>All outcomes as text</summary><p>With no change, both methods return 103 and 105. After 101 is cancelled, OFFSET 2 returns 105 and 106, skipping 103; the saved key returns 103 and 105. If 103’s time moves to 13 October 12:00 UTC, the list becomes 101, 103, 102, 105, 106. OFFSET 2 repeats 102 and returns 105. The saved key returns 105 and 106, but misses the moved 103. These are independent illustrative histories, with cancelled orders excluded from the list.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-continuation]').forEach(root=>{
 const change=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-change]')!,method=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-method]')!;
 const draw=()=>{const c=change.value,k=method.value==='key',ids=c==='cancel'?[102,103,105,106]:c==='move'?[101,103,102,105,106]:[101,102,103,105,106];
 root.querySelectorAll<HTMLLIElement>('[data-orders] li').forEach((li,index)=>{const id=ids[index];li.hidden=id===undefined;li.removeAttribute('aria-label');if(id!==undefined){li.textContent=String(id);if(id===102)li.setAttribute('aria-label','102, saved boundary');}});
 root.querySelector('[data-answer]')!.textContent=c==='none'?'103, 105':c==='cancel'?(k?'103, 105':'105, 106'):(k?'105, 106':'102, 105');
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=c==='none'?'The list has not changed. Skipping two rows and continuing after order 102 return the same next two orders.':c==='cancel'?(k?'Cancelling 101 did not change the saved key. Continue after 102: 103 and 105 still qualify.':'After 101 leaves, the first two rows are 102 and 103. OFFSET 2 skips them both, so 103 is never delivered.'):(k?'Order 103 moved behind the saved boundary. Continuing after that boundary cannot recover it; a keyset is not a frozen result.':'Order 103 moved between 101 and 102. Skipping two rows now starts at 102 again, repeating a delivered order and missing 103.');
 };change.addEventListener('change',draw);method.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();
 });
</script>
<style>
.continuation{margin:2.5rem 0;padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);font:.92rem/1.6 var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font-size:1.08rem;margin-bottom:1rem}figcaption span{font-size:.75rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;margin-right:.6rem}.choices{display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap}.choices label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem}select{font:inherit;padding:.5rem;max-width:100%;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border-radius:.25rem}select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}.current{margin:1rem 0}.current p,.answer p{margin-bottom:.4rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.8rem}ol{list-style:none;padding:0;display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap}li{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:.6rem .8rem}li[aria-label]{border:2px solid var(--color-accent);font-weight:650}.answer{padding:.8rem;border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong)}.answer strong{font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--color-accent)}[data-explanation]{border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.7rem;min-height:6em}details{font-size:.85rem}
</style>
